
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

## Host unit tests (`test_gyro`)

The gyro controllers (`GyroStraight`, `GyroTurn`) are pure C++ with no Arduino
dependencies, so they are tested on the host with PlatformIO's `native` env:

```bash
pio test -e native
```

The `native` env compiles only `GyroStraight.cpp` and `GyroTurn.cpp` (see
`build_src_filter`) and needs a host `gcc`/`g++` on `PATH`. If you don't have
one, install PlatformIO's MinGW toolchain and add it to `PATH` for the run:

```powershell
pio pkg install -g -t platformio/toolchain-gccmingw32
$env:PATH = "$env:USERPROFILE\.platformio\packages\toolchain-gccmingw32\bin;$env:PATH"
pio test -e native
```
